<section class="section-pad">
  <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem;">

    <!-- Eyebrow (2.5): renamed from "The hook" to an in-world label that
         fits what this section is actually about — friends spending vault
         cards to raise the stakes on your next draw. -->
    <p class="fade-in" style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.28em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#A84D30;margin:0 0 1.25rem;text-align:center;">
      The wager
    </p>

    <!-- H2 -->
    <h2 class="fade-in" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:#2E2115;margin:0 0 2rem;text-align:center;">
      Your friends believe you can handle more.
    </h2>

    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="fade-in" style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;color:#766449;max-width:600px;margin:0 auto 2.5rem;">
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.25em;">
        Every morning you draw five cards at random from five categories: Physical, Mental, Nutrition, Recovery, and Wildcard. You look at the hand, decide what you can handle, and commit.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.25em;">
        Once you commit, those cards are locked. No one can touch them while you work or after you finish. Your cards are yours.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.25em;">
        Tomorrow's draw is a different story. Your friends earn cards of their own by finishing their own habits, and they can spend one on you before you wake up. They might swap a harder card into your hand, lock in one commitment before you've seen the rest, or hide the whole draw so you choose blind. They might also leave you something better than what you would have drawn.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0;">
        So some mornings you wake up to a card you never would have picked for yourself, and you do it anyway. That is the practice.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2.13: a stated rule, not a quotation — a small parchment plaque
         instead of an italic blockquote with quote marks. -->
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;">
      <div class="fade-in rule-plaque warm-shadow">
        <span class="rule-plaque-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p class="rule-plaque-text">Completed cards are immune. That's the deal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .rule-plaque {
    max-width: 460px;
    background: #FDF7EA;
    border: 1px solid rgba(199, 91, 57, 0.3);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .rule-plaque-mark {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 28px;
    height: 2px;
    background: #C75B39;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .rule-plaque-text {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.8vw, 1.4rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #2E2115;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
